{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["<a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/inoue0426/llm-tuning-playground/blob/main/notebooks/05_grpo_drug_target_retrieval.ipynb\" target=\"_parent\"><img src=\"https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg\" alt=\"Open In Colab\"/></a>\n","\n","# 05 - GRPO with a drug-target reward\n","\n","This experiment turns a drug-target interaction table into a small dictionary-like benchmark and uses GRPO with a verifiable reward. The reward is computed by exact matching the predicted target against a held-out drug->target dictionary.\n","\n","**Important:** this notebook uses the private `inoue0426/drugbank_dti` repository as a research data source. It does not copy the source table into this public repository. The notebook downloads the CSV at runtime from a GitHub raw URL, so access must be available to the runtime. Treat the source data as governed by its original terms.\n","\n","The goal is to learn the GRPO mechanics, not to claim clinical or biomedical validity."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["!pip -q install -U \\\n","    \"transformers>=4.55,<5\" \\\n","    \"datasets>=3.6,<5\" \\\n","    \"peft>=0.17,<1\" \\\n","    \"trl>=0.29,<1\" \\\n","    \"accelerate>=1.10,<2\" \\\n","    \"bitsandbytes>=0.46,<1\" \\\n","    \"torchao>=0.16,<1\""]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["import ast\n","import pandas as pd\n","import torch\n","from datasets import Dataset\n","\n","import transformers, datasets, peft, trl\n","print('PyTorch:', torch.__version__)\n","print('Transformers:', transformers.__version__)\n","print('Datasets:', datasets.__version__)\n","print('PEFT:', peft.__version__)\n","print('TRL:', trl.__version__)\n","print('CUDA available:', torch.cuda.is_available())\n","if not torch.cuda.is_available():\n","    raise RuntimeError('Select a GPU runtime in Colab before running this notebook.')\n","print('GPU:', torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n","print('VRAM (GB):', round(torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1024**3, 1))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Load the drug-target table at runtime\n","\n","The source repository contains `drug_bank.csv` with drug names, DrugBank IDs, target names, target UniProt IDs, and optional chemical identifiers. We build a compact one-target-per-example dictionary from the source data."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["import io\n","import requests\n","\n","SOURCE_URL = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/inoue0426/drugbank_dti/main/drug_bank.csv'\n","r = requests.get(SOURCE_URL, timeout=60)\n","r.raise_for_status()\n","df = pd.read_csv(io.BytesIO(r.content))\n","\n","print('Rows:', len(df))\n","print('Columns:', list(df.columns))\n","df.head()"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["# Build a dictionary: drug name -> list of target UniProt IDs and names.\n","drug_targets = {}\n","for _, row in df.iterrows():\n","    drug = str(row['Drug Name']).strip()\n","    try:\n","        target_ids = ast.literal_eval(str(row['Targets']))\n","    except Exception:\n","        target_ids = []\n","    try:\n","        target_names = ast.literal_eval(str(row['Targets Name']))\n","    except Exception:\n","        target_names = []\n","    pairs = list(zip(target_ids, target_names))\n","    if drug and pairs:\n","        drug_targets[drug] = pairs\n","\n","# Keep drugs with exactly one target for this first GRPO experiment.\nsingle_target = {d: pairs[0] for d, pairs in drug_targets.items() if len(pairs) == 1}\n","print('Drugs with exactly one target:', len(single_target))\n","list(single_target.items())[:10]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Create a compact prompt-only GRPO dataset\n","\n","GRPO expects prompt-only data. The gold target is kept in an additional column and passed to the reward function. The model must return a target UniProt ID, e.g. `P00734`. TRL passes custom dataset columns to reward functions.\n","\n","We split by drug so the evaluation set contains unseen drugs."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["items = list(single_target.items())\n","\n","records = []\n","for drug, (target_id, target_name) in items:\n","    records.append({\n","        'prompt': [\n","            {'role': 'user', 'content':\n","             f'What is the protein target UniProt ID for the drug {drug}? Reply with the UniProt ID only.'}\n","        ],\n","        'drug': drug,\n","        'target_id': target_id,\n","        'target_name': target_name,\n","    })\n","\n","dataset = Dataset.from_list(records).shuffle(seed=42)\n","split = dataset.train_test_split(test_size=0.2, seed=42)\n","train_dataset = split['train']\n","eval_dataset = split['test']\n","\n","print('Total:', len(dataset))\n","print('Train:', len(train_dataset))\n","print('Eval:', len(eval_dataset))\n","print(train_dataset[0])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Load a small instruct model\n","\n","We use Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct to keep the Colab experiment lightweight. This is intentionally a toy-scale RL experiment."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n","\n","MODEL_NAME = 'Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct'\n","tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME)\n","if tokenizer.pad_token is None:\n","    tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n","tokenizer.padding_side = 'left'\n","\n","dtype = torch.bfloat16 if torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported() else torch.float16\n","model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME, torch_dtype=dtype)\n","model = model.cuda()"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["def generate_answer(model, drug):\n","    messages = [{'role':'user','content': f'What is the protein target UniProt ID for the drug {drug}? Reply with the UniProt ID only.'}]\n","    encoded = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(messages, tokenize=True, add_generation_prompt=True, return_tensors='pt', return_dict=True)\n","    encoded = {k: v.to(model.device) for k, v in encoded.items()}\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        output = model.generate(**encoded, max_new_tokens=16, do_sample=False, pad_token_id=tokenizer.pad_token_id)\n","    return tokenizer.decode(output[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n","\n","print('BEFORE GRPO')\n","for i in range(min(5, len(eval_dataset))):\n","    print('Drug:', eval_dataset[i]['drug'])\n","    print(generate_answer(model, eval_dataset[i]['drug']))\n","    print('Gold:', eval_dataset[i]['target_id'])\n","    print()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Reward function\n","\n","This is the key GRPO idea: instead of `chosen/rejected`, the model generates an answer and we compute a scalar reward from a verifier. Here the verifier is an exact lookup against the source dictionary.\n","\n","Reward = 1 if the generated text contains the correct UniProt ID, otherwise 0."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["import re\n","\n","def target_reward(completions, target_id, **kwargs):\n","    rewards = []\n","    for completion, gold in zip(completions, target_id):\n","        text = completion[0]['content'] if isinstance(completion, list) else str(completion)\n","        found = re.findall(r'\\b[A-Z][0-9][A-Z0-9]{3}[0-9]\\b', text.upper())\n","        rewards.append(1.0 if str(gold).upper() in found else 0.0)\n","    return rewards"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. GRPO training\n","\n","GRPO uses multiple sampled completions per prompt and optimizes their relative rewards. We use LoRA to keep the trainable parameter count small.\n","\n","Because this is a first experiment, the number of steps and generations per prompt are intentionally small."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["from peft import LoraConfig\n","from trl import GRPOConfig, GRPOTrainer\n","\n","lora_config = LoraConfig(\n","    r=8,\n","    lora_alpha=16,\n","    lora_dropout=0.05,\n","    target_modules=['q_proj','k_proj','v_proj','o_proj'],\n","    bias='none',\n","    task_type='CAUSAL_LM',\n",")\n","\n","grpo_args = GRPOConfig(\n","    output_dir='./outputs/drug-target-grpo',\n","    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n","    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n","    learning_rate=5e-6,\n","    max_steps=100,\n","    num_generations=4,\n","    max_prompt_length=128,\n","    max_completion_length=16,\n","    logging_steps=10,\n","    save_strategy='no',\n","    report_to='none',\n","    use_vllm=False,\n","    fp16=torch.cuda.is_available() and not torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n","    bf16=torch.cuda.is_available() and torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",")\n","\n","trainer = GRPOTrainer(\n","    model=model,\n","    args=grpo_args,\n","    train_dataset=train_dataset,\n","    eval_dataset=eval_dataset,\n","    processing_class=tokenizer,\n","    reward_funcs=target_reward,\n","    peft_config=lora_config,\n")\n","trainer.train()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. After-GRPO evaluation\n","\n","The strict evaluation is drug-disjoint: the drugs in `eval_dataset` were not used for training. A hit requires an exact match to the gold UniProt target ID."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["def extract_target(text):\n","    found = re.findall(r'\\b[A-Z][0-9][A-Z0-9]{3}[0-9]\\b', text.upper())\n","    return found[0] if found else None\n","\n","def exact_accuracy(model, dataset):\n","    correct = 0\n","    rows = []\n","    for ex in dataset:\n","        text = generate_answer(model, ex['drug'])\n","        pred = extract_target(text)\n","        ok = pred == ex['target_id'].upper()\n","        correct += int(ok)\n","        rows.append((ex['drug'], ex['target_id'], pred, ok))\n","    acc = correct / len(dataset) if len(dataset) else float('nan')\n","    return acc, rows\n","\n","print('AFTER GRPO')\n","after_acc, after_rows = exact_accuracy(model, eval_dataset)\n","print(f'Exact target accuracy: {after_acc:.3f}')\n","for drug, gold, pred, ok in after_rows[:10]:\n","    print(f'{drug}: gold={gold}, pred={pred}, correct={ok}')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Before vs After\n","\n","This compares exact target retrieval on the same drug-disjoint evaluation set."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"source":["before_acc = 0.0\n","before_rows = []\n","# The notebook did not save the base model separately. For a strict before/after comparison,\n","# reload the original base model and evaluate it on the same held-out drugs.\n","base_model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME, torch_dtype=dtype).cuda()\n","before_acc, before_rows = exact_accuracy(base_model, eval_dataset)\n","\n","print('Base accuracy :', f'{before_acc:.3f}')\n","print('GRPO accuracy  :', f'{after_acc:.3f}')\n","print('Absolute gain  :', f'{after_acc - before_acc:+.3f}')\n","\n","del base_model\n","torch.cuda.empty_cache()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## What this experiment demonstrates\n","\n","DPO learns from an explicit preference pair. GRPO instead samples candidate answers and learns from a reward verifier. Here the verifier is a deterministic drug-target lookup.\n","\n","This is intentionally simple. A stronger biomedical experiment would use hard negatives, multiple valid targets, target-family ambiguity handling, and a drug-disjoint evaluation protocol. It would also keep any licensed source data outside this public repository.\n","\n","## Next ideas\n","\n","- Reward based on a set of valid targets rather than one target.\n","- Partial credit for target-family or entity resolution.\n","- Add a format reward for producing only a UniProt ID.\n","- Use a public/redistributable DTI benchmark for a fully reproducible public version.\n"]}],"metadata":{"accelerator":"GPU","colab":{"name":"05_grpo_drug_target_retrieval.ipynb","provenance":[],"gpuType":"L4"},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}